The files in the MD folder are needed to compute the MD descriptors.
Dependencies: Amber, Gromacs, Plumed

First, the users have to execute the .sh scripts from 1- to 8-:
1-image_from_dcd_drug: creates a new trajectory file including the pre-production and production steps
2-save_drug: creates a trajectory file containing only the centered and aligned drug molecule
3-extract_average: extracts the average structure of the ligand from the imaged trajectory
4-extract_clos_to_avg: extracts the conformation closest to average structure of the ligand from the imaged trajectory
5-watershell: generates the solvation files for computing the solvation shell
6-hbonds: computes the hydrogen bond files for computing the hydrogen bond descriptors
7-cluster: generates the conformational clusters of the drug molecules
8-plumed-gromacs: computes the RMSF, the asphericity, acylindricity, and kappa2 descriptors (it needs the plumed.inp input file)

After executing all the scripts, the users can use extract_MD_descr.sh file, to extract all MD descriptors.
